25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It appears that tools requiring universal daily entry tend to fail, while narrow, trade-specific tools endure. Standardization often fails without a clear owner.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital line is frozen, but we have some room in the software allowance. Also, fixed-fee work is more stable than per-head licensing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh no! Network coverage at customer plants is terrible, and getting devices approved takes forever. But vendor queries are just repetitive requests.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"We are losing an hour daily to copying records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because different units have different addresses for the same firm.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Our developers are busy until the third quarter, and the coordination group is severely understaffed, with two people doing everything by hand.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, your finding about duplicate records is interesting. It suggests a systemic failure in how we store basic information.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Asuka, if the developers are busy... does that mean we can't build anything new right now?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, the misrouted deliveries sound like a mystery! Maybe we need a better way to share addresses?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Precisely, Sakura. The inefficiency is tangible and happens every single day on the floor.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Daisuke, it means any project requiring heavy internal coding is a risk. We would be dependent on an overstretched team or undocumented interfaces.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must be wary of ""grand"" projects. As I saw, the narrow tools are the ones that actually survive.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried about the costs. If we use per-head licenses, the bill might grow too large for our allowance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Asuka, if the coordination group is so tired, maybe we should find something that helps them specifically?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with Servas. We should solve a concrete, daily problem rather than chasing a broad organizational dream.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Sakura, helping the coordination group is a good goal, but not if it adds more manual work to their plate.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
