50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A: Supplier Data Hub, B: Workflow Assistant, C: Training Studio, and D: Field Service App. I lean toward A.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"A seems useful, but will it use per-head licenses? B might be cheaper, but I'm not sure.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Sakura,,I can't support D! The network coverage is too bad for a mobile app to work reliably.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,A directly addresses the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. It is the most logical choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"B and D would likely require too much from our developers or the coordination group. A is a repository, which is more stable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, do you think A avoids the ""daily entry"" trap that killed previous rollouts?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If A is a central catalog, maybe it doesn't need everyone to enter data every day?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, if A fixes the address problem, the deliveries will stop getting lost! That's like solving a puzzle!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Yes, Sakura. It replaces fragmented records with a single source of truth.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"As long as it's a searchable catalog with shared procedures, it's less burdensome than a workflow tool like B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,A aligns with the success of the tool room walkthroughs—it provides a lasting resource.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel more comfortable with A if it helps the company save time and avoids the frozen capital budget.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I vote for A! It's the most helpful for everyone.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for A. It solves the most pressing operational failures.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I vote for A. It is the most realistic given our staffing constraints.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Servas,,I also vote for A. It is the most prudent investment.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for A too.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
